% Matrix role (HZ): Z-type stabilizer parity-check matrix H_Z = [ R(b)^T | L(a)^T ] (shape l x 2l; detects X errors).
%   Paired with finG=<tag>_HX.mtx (or finL=<tag>_LZ.mtx) in dist_m4ri to compute d_X.
%
% 2BGA CSS Construction (Lin & Pryadko, Phys. Rev. A 109, 022407 (2024); search_2bga.py):
%   Qubits 1..135 are block L (F_2[G]); qubits 136..270 are block R (F_2[G]).
%   H_X = [ L(a) | R(b) ] and H_Z = [ R(b)^T | L(a)^T ], where [L(a)]_{alpha,beta} = 1 iff
%   alpha = g * beta (g in a) and [R(b)]_{alpha,beta} = 1 iff alpha = beta * h (h in b).
%   Since G is abelian, R(b) = L(b), H_X * H_Z^T = 0 (mod 2), and X<->Z exchange with
%   block swap + group inversion g -> g^-1 is a code automorphism, so d_X = d_Z = d.
%   Group G = SmallGroup(135, 2) =~ C_45 x C_3 (order l = 135, abelian):
%     * Direct-product generators: x = Elements(G)[8] = f1 * f3 (order 45),
%       y = Elements(G)[3] = f2 (order 3), with x^45 = y^3 = 1 and x y = y x.
%     * Bivariate polynomials in F_2[x,y]/(x^45-1, y^3-1): a(x,y) = 1 + x^5y + x^8y^2 + x^30 + x^30y^2 + x^44y
%       and b(x,y) = 1 + x^8 + x^18 + x^26y + x^29y + x^39.
%     * GAP Elements(SmallGroup(135, 2)) basis order (rows/cols 1..135 of each block):
%       Pcgs(G) = [f1, f2, f3, f4] = [x^10, y, x^36, x^30] (rel. orders [3, 3, 5, 3],
%       f1^3 = f4; GAP indices 2, 3, 4, 5). List e = (e1,e2,e3,e4) in Z_3xZ_3xZ_5xZ_3
%       sorted by (e1+e2+e3+e4, -e1, -e2, -e3, -e4); k-th element (1..135) is
%       f1^e1 * f2^e2 * f3^e3 * f4^e4 = x^((10*e1 + 36*e3 + 30*e4) mod 45) * y^e2.
%     * a indices -> e1e2e3e4: 1:0000, 5:0001, 26:0201, 35:2101, 132:2232, 133:2142
